tools/mesa: the viewport row (L74) -- what size the client thinks it renders at

Why: M3's 720p run reported "surface 1920x1080" while its `[XSW] w=` said
1280x720, and nothing in the row set could say whether the *viewport* had also
stayed at desktop size.  Three facts decide whether a resolution is real:

  glViewport(x,y,w,h)                -- this row
  the drawable the frontend hands the winsys ([VGL] res_create ... dt)
  the rect the shim blits into /dev/fb0 ([XSW] ... w= h= gx= gy=)

They are produced by three different layers, so they can disagree, and a
"720p" number that is really a 1080p surface is exactly what M3 measured
(15.97 fps at 1916x1018 vs 12.15 fps for a 720p request that was still
rendering 1920x1080).

Bounded and opt-in: four rows, then one per change, capped at 64, and only
when HOBBYOS_GL_VIEWPORT is in the environment (rwlaunch exports it from the
/VPON marker).  It is a switch of its own and not part of HOBBYOS_GLX_TRACE
because that trace prints a row per glX call and would perturb the fps it is
measuring.  The shipped DSO pays one predictable branch per glViewport.

--- a/src/mesa/main/viewport.c
+++ b/src/mesa/main/viewport.c
@@ -134,6 +134,37 @@
    viewport(ctx, x, y, width, height);
 }
 
+/* HOBBYOS (L74): the viewport row.
+ *
+ * The question "is the GL surface really the size the window asked for?" has
+ * three answers and they can disagree: what the client passed to glViewport,
+ * the drawable size the frontend hands the winsys (a pipe_resource of that
+ * size, logged as [VGL] res_create), and the rect the shim blits into
+ * /dev/fb0 ([XSW] w=/h=/gx=/gy=).  This is the first of the three.  Bounded:
+ * the first four calls, then only when the rect changes, capped at 64, and
+ * only when HOBBYOS_GL_VIEWPORT is set (rwlaunch exports it from /VPON).  It
+ * is a switch of its own, not part of HOBBYOS_GLX_TRACE, because that trace
+ * prints a row per glX call and would perturb a measured fps run.  The
+ * shipped DSO pays one predictable branch per call.
+ */
+static void
+hobbyos_viewport_row(GLint x, GLint y, GLsizei w, GLsizei h)
+{
+   static int on = -1;
+   static int nx = -1, ny = -1, nw = -1, nh = -1;
+   static unsigned rows;
+   if (on < 0)
+      on = getenv("HOBBYOS_GL_VIEWPORT") ? 1 : 0;
+   if (!on)
+      return;
+   if ((rows < 4 || x != nx || y != ny || w != nw || h != nh) && rows < 64) {
+      fprintf(stderr, "[GL] viewport x=%d y=%d w=%d h=%d\n",
+              (int)x, (int)y, (int)w, (int)h);
+      rows++;
+   }
+   nx = (int)x; ny = (int)y; nw = (int)w; nh = (int)h;
+}
+
 void GLAPIENTRY
 _mesa_Viewport(GLint x, GLint y, GLsizei width, GLsizei height)
 {
@@ -145,6 +176,7 @@
       return;
    }
 
+   hobbyos_viewport_row(x, y, width, height);
    viewport(ctx, x, y, width, height);
 }
 
